From 1e5f9f7513f8ccf25ca71b841c9cbc353e47852c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:23:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sessions): preserve human GUI visibility across local
 routing [daveey]

Canonical session.create(gui) freezes GUI policy and persists desktop creation
provenance. Peer refresh changes routing source to local without changing that
provenance. The human-only Desktop project/list classifier recognized neither
gui nor the mixed local routing class, so real interactive chats disappeared
outside the pinned section.

Treat gui as the desktop surface and consult recognized creation provenance
only for local routing. Explicit automated deny and wildcard rules retain
precedence; local bot/eval/oneshot/unknown remain automated. Apply the same
source/provenance exclusions in SQL before list pagination and total counts,
including pinned backfill, instead of excluding the entire local routing class.
No source relabeling, backfill, live session mutation or renderer change.

Regression proof covers authenticated canonical GUI create, durable provenance,
real peer refresh, resume, compression publication, project projection and both
paged REST list routes. Main fails these regressions; patched suites pass:
60 focused tests and 250 imported-module consumers. Full scripts/check passes
21 checks. Independent review and required exact-head CI remain landing gates.

Five whys: normal project rows missing because automated filter hid them;
classifier used mutable routing source instead of creation surface; canonical
gui alias/local refresh were absent from the human allowlist; source-only SQL
also discarded mixed routing classes before pagination; initial admission proof
did not inspect actual renderer grouping. Temporary pins are containment only.
